            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I think most plugins shouldn't need to care about this until it is something like [multicursor.nvim](https://github.com/jake-stewart/multicursor.nvim).\n\nIn general, the idea is:\n\n1. Disable \"following\" mode.\n2. Change the cursor.\n3. Restore \"following\" mode (what exactly should be restored?)\n\nThis is already how `/` searching works with \"following\" mode enabled: it only moves the main cursor. A similar use case could be 2d jumping.\n\nI can also imagine [multicursor.nvim](https://github.com/jake-stewart/multicursor.nvim) relying on this, but I'm not sure whether this would be enough for plugins like that.",
