        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I assume `vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor` will move all cursors when \"following\" mode is enabled. If so, plugins like [mini.jump2d](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.jump2d) might want to prevent cascading even when \"following\" mode is enabled. But to be honest, this is mostly speculation on my part, so I hope some real-world use cases come up.\n\nTechnically, multicursor mode can be disabled with `<C-l>` and restored with `gQ`, but by default `gQ` doesn't restore the follow-mode.\n\nP.S. I guess deleting all cursors disables follow-mode automatically.",
