            "body": "> sticky cursor, like in the example here: https://github.com/jake-stewart/multicursor.nvim/wiki/More-examples#sticky-cursor ... I need to move the cursor with `api.nvim_win_set_cursor()`\n\nNot sure what that video is showing, but `nvim_win_set_cursor` in a mapping already cascades, and is repeatable, which is what https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41675 addressed. Would help to see a concrete example (using Nvim 0.13 features, not the multicursor.nvim wiki).\n\n\nAlso for reference it looks like your \"sticky cursor\" is unrelated to the \"sticky cursor\" mentioned here:\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/discussions/41819\n\n\n",
