            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I kinda have the code right from the oven, but it might be a bit confusing since I haven't put much thought into it.\n\nThe idea is for `<C-S-j/k>` to always extend the cursor, regardless of the current follow mode. The behavior changes depending on the follow mode, but it doesn't actually rely on cursor following, more like I'm building different behavior based on the mode flag. In both modes, the cursor extends in the given direction, but when follow mode is enabled, it prefers to jump&delete the next cursor if there is one (what I call a sticky cursor).\n\n### What\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5c40ab4a-6001-4807-bb75-b9a3eb06edcf\n\n### How\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/discussions/41997",
